  "title": "Bellier et al. 2023 Pink Floyd music listening ECoG: authors' high-frequency activity (HFA, 70-150 Hz) for 29 patients",
  "description": "A BIDS-packaged derivative dataset of high-frequency activity (HFA, 70-150 Hz) estimates at 100 Hz, recorded with electrocorticography (ECoG) from 29 patients with pharmacoresistant epilepsy while they passively listened to Pink Floyd's 'Another Brick in the Wall, Part 1'. It includes electrode coordinates in MNI space and the authors' flags for noisy and epileptic channels. Raw ECoG recordings and the stimulus audio are not included.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG was recorded at 1200 Hz with g.USBamp amplifiers and BCI2000 at Albany Medical Center, using clinical Ad-Tech grids and strips covering the superior temporal gyrus. HFA was extracted by notch filtering, 1 Hz high-pass filtering, and band-passing into 20-Hz sub-bands between 70 and 150 Hz. Each sub-band was median common-average referenced, and its Hilbert envelope was taken and robust-scaled. The sub-bands were averaged and the result downsampled to 100 Hz.",
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
